.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt BFCTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bfctl
.Nd manage World of Warcraft addons reproducibly
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Fl -path Ar root
.Nm
.Cm add Ar source Op Fl -flavor Ar flavor Op Fl -branch Ar branch Op Fl -strategy Cm release Op Fl -force
.Nm
.Cm remove Ar id Op Fl -flavor Ar flavor
.Nm
.Cm sync
.Op Fl -check-only
.Op Fl -explain
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -offline
.Nm
.Cm status
.Fl -scan Ar dir
.Op Fl -flavor Ar flavor Fl -interface Ar number
.Nm
.Cm tui
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a reproducible, offline-friendly World of Warcraft addon manager for
Linux clients.
It discovers client flavors
.Pq mainline, forever, classic, mists; camelot is an accepted spelling of forever ,
tracks addons by GitHub repository
.Pq stable releases, a branch, or a pinned release or tag ,
by Wago Addons page slug or ID, or by any git remote,
installs them atomically through a transactional installer with rollback,
and resolves multi-TOC layouts with the packaging rules used upstream
.Pq .pkgmeta, -classic/-bcc/-wrath suffixes .
.Pp
A bare
.Nm
on a terminal opens the interactive manager; in scripts and pipes it prints
the usage text and exits 2.
Use
.Cm tui
to open the UI explicitly.
.Pp
Global flags:
.Fl v , -verbose
raise log detail,
.Fl q , -quiet
silences normal logging.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "status"
.It Cm init Fl -path Ar root
Create the
.Nm
configuration layout and register the client flavor installed under
.Ar root ,
for example
.Pa ~/Games/World of Warcraft/_forever_ .
.It Cm add Ar source
Add and install an addon from a GitHub repository
.Pq Ar owner/repo
or a full URL, a Wago Addons reference
.Pq the addon page URL or Ar wago:key ,
a CurseForge reference
.Pq the addon page URL or Ar cfwidget:key ,
or any other git remote URL.
An addon added via Wago stays maintained through Wago;
an addon added via CurseForge stays maintained through
the cfwidget mirror and installs from CurseForge's open CDN.
For a flavor the author ships only on a lower CurseForge channel
.Pq e.g. Forever builds published as beta ,
the most stable channel serving the flavor is taken: release, then beta, then alpha.
.Fl -branch Ar branch
tracks a development branch instead of stable releases;
.Fl -strategy Cm release
pins to GitHub releases and silences the staleness detector.
.Fl -flavor
selects the client when several are configured;
.Cm camelot
is accepted as a spelling of
.Cm forever .
.Fl -force
takes over addon directories owned by another addon.
.It Cm remove Ar id
Remove the addon's owned directories and drop its manifest entry, atomically.
.It Cm adopt
Take over an existing addon installation: bind its directories to bfctl
management, or re-bind an addon installed by a foreign tool.
.It Cm sync
Resolve every managed addon against its upstream and install updates.
Addons are worked concurrently and their results are reported in report
order.
An update is the matching release asset when one serves the client, and a
local source build
.Pq .pkgmeta externals, keyword substitution, TOC flavor split
when no asset does or the releases are stale.
Never prompts: suitable for launch scripts and cron.
.Fl -check-only
reports without downloading,
.Fl -explain
annotates the resolution reason of each plan,
.Fl -json
prints a machine-readable report.
.It Cm status
Show one table per client flavor:
Addons, installed versions, strategies, owned directories, TOC
compatibility and the last upstream tag.
.Fl -json
prints a machine-readable report,
.Fl -offline
drops the Upstream column.
.Fl -scan Ar dir
lists a bare AddOns directory with its selected .toc files and compatibility
verdicts
.Pq Fl -flavor Ns / Ns Fl -interface pin the target client .
.It Cm tui
Open the interactive addon manager: an addon table
.Pq Addon, Installed, Upstream, Strategy, Status
with a styled header bar
.Pq flavor badge, game version, root and live counts ,
status and help bars, and a detail pane that is persistent beside the
table on wide terminals
.Pq at least 120 columns ,
and a toggle overlay below it on narrow ones.
Columns are sized from the terminal; truncated cells show their full
value in the detail pane.
Statuses carry a glyph and a word
.Pq green up to date, yellow update available, red failed/Missing, dim manual ,
and color never carries meaning alone.
Keys:
.Ar u
update all,
.Ar s
toggle release/branch tracking,
.Ar d
delete with confirmation,
.Ar a
add an addon
.Pq inline ref input, validated live; several configured clients ask for the target flavor ,
.Ar enter
detail pane toggle,
.Ar /
filter
.Pq matches name and source; esc clears ,
.Ar o
cycle sort
.Pq name / status / upstream ,
.Ar ?
full help overlay
.Pq every key grouped by context; closed with ? or esc ,
.Ar q
quit
.Pq asks for confirmation while a sync or add is in flight, stating that quitting rolls back the in-flight install ,
.Ar ctrl+c
cancel the running sync
.Pq with rollback
and then offer quit.
An add flow is cancelled with
.Ar esc .
.Fl -ascii
degrades every glyph, border and separator to plain ASCII on
non-UTF-8 terminals
.Pq which are detected via LANG/LC_ALL; the status glyphs become + ! x * .
.It Cm version
Print version information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Runtime failure, or an interrupted sync
.Pq its in-flight install was rolled back .
.It 2
Usage error.
.It 4
.Pq Cm sync
partial failure: some addons failed
.El
.Sh JSON OUTPUT
.Cm status Fl -json
prints an object with a flat
.Va addons
array and a
.Va clients
grouping; each addon carries
.Va flavor , id , name , installed , upstream , strategy , tracking , status , dirs , sourceKind , source .
.Cm sync Fl -json
prints
.Va results
per addon
.Pq Va flavor , addon , status , from , to , reason , error
and an aggregate
.Va summary .
Both are stable interfaces intended for
.Xr jq 1 .
.Sh PROGRESS OUTPUT
While
.Cm sync , Cm add
or
.Cm adopt
works, ongoing activity is reported on standard error as it happens.
.Cm sync
works on several addons at once, and on a terminal every addon owns one
row of a live block
.Pq spinner, rewritten in place
that is visible from the start and tracks its own addon through the
phases, flipping in place to its terminal line when the addon finishes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
syncing: <index>/<total> <flavor>/<addon>: <phase>
done: <index>/<total> <flavor>/<addon>: <version>
.Ed
.Pp
The row's verb names the flow
.Pq Ar syncing , adding , adopting ;
the terminal phase replaces it with
.Ar done , failed
or
.Ar skipped ,
and the addon's result line then replaces that row outright, so every
addon's whole story stays in one place.
A rate-limit wait appends its reason to the row while it lasts.
.Pp
The block adapts to its terminal: on non-UTF-8 terminals the spinner
falls back to plain ASCII frames
.Pq Ar LC_ALL , LC_CTYPE , LANG
are consulted, in that order,
no color is drawn when
.Ev NO_COLOR
is set
.Pq the words carry the meaning either way ,
and every row is clamped to the terminal width, so a long version string
can never wrap and disturb the redraw.
.Pp
Over a pipe
.Pq CI log, file
the same work streams as one incremental plain line per event, without
ANSI or other control bytes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
progress: <index>/<total> <flavor>/<addon>: <phase>[: <detail>]
.Ed
.Pp
.Ar phase
is one of
.Ar resolving , downloading , installing , done , failed , skipped ;
.Ar detail
names the version or ref in flight, the failure or skip reason, or a
rate-limit wait.
.Fl q , -quiet
suppresses progress entirely.
.Pp
Stream discipline: results and the
.Fl -json
report stay alone on standard output; progress and logs use standard
error.
The per-addon result lines and the summary keep their historical format,
and the result lines always stream in report order even though the work
runs in parallel, so
.Nm
output is safe to pipe
.Pq e.g. into jq
or capture.
On
.Dv SIGINT
the rows in flight are kept as they are and the cursor restored before
the rollback
message prints
.Pq see Sx SIGNALS .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGINT
.It Dv SIGINT
Cancels an in-flight sync
.Pq or an in-flight TUI update
through the installer's rollback: completed work is kept, the interrupted
install is rolled back and
.Nm
exits 1.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.config/bfctl/state.json"
.It Pa ~/.config/bfctl/state.json
Lock-protected manifest: tracked addons, sources, strategies.
.It Pa ~/.config/bfctl/config.yaml
Optional user configuration
.Pq e.g. staleness_days .
.It Pa ~/.cache/bfctl
Resolved metadata cache
.Pq content-addressed blobs and unpacked trees .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width GH_TOKEN
.It Ev GH_TOKEN , GITHUB_TOKEN
Optional GitHub personal access token sent as a bearer token on every API
request, raising the rate limit from 60 to 5000 requests per hour.
GH_TOKEN takes precedence over GITHUB_TOKEN; any classic token suffices for
public repositories.
Never written to logs or state.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , XDG_CACHE_HOME , BFCTL_CONFIG_HOME , BFCTL_CACHE_HOME
Override the default directories.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Register the
.Em forever
flavor and track a stable-release addon:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bfctl init --path ~/Games/World of Warcraft/_forever_
bfctl add owner/repo
bfctl sync --check-only
bfctl status
.Ed
.Pp
JSON for scripting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bfctl status --json | jq -r '.addons[] | [.name, .status] | @tsv'
.Ed
.Pp
Launch script
.Pq no prompts, deterministic exit codes :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bfctl sync || case $? in 4) echo "partial failure" ;; *) exit ;; esac
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dwarves 7
